azgor wrote:
> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
> freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

Thanks for posting these!  Been missing them.

> [1]: Nurses should sometimes carry stethoscopes. --lament

This would make stethoscopes less rare, lessening one of the
differentiations of the healer class.  But stethoscopes are fairly
low-use items anyway.  The only real objection I have is, isn't it
doctors that use stethoscopes in RL, instead of nurses?

> [2]: Spellcasters (the Wizard class) should gain a bonus to all spells
> (be it a bonus to damage, bonus to healing, etc..) when casting while
> not wielding a weapon. This bonus should increase by +1 every 5 XL.
> --aristotle73

Not fond of this one.  It's such a simple matter to unwield your
weapon, especially now we have the eXchange command, so once you cancel
fractions, for anyone who knows the lore this idea is equal to "make
spells more powerful."  There might be merit in that, but I'm not fond
of the unwield rigamarole.  (Even if it would open up so many lovely
cockatrice-related deaths....)

> [3]: In reference to Ideas[2], perhaps several different classes should
> each have bonuses to a single spell category; e.g. priests to clerical,
> healers to healing, rogues to escape, etc. --PsyMar

This is already covered, to a large degree, by the spell skill system.

> [4]: Elven weapons enchantable to +9. Why does only armor get the
> bonus? --jmr

I like the idea of raising the safe enchantment limit (with appropriate
drawbacks of course), for all weapons and armor.  I think I'm in favor
of this idea, even considering the possible abuse it opens up.  (Step
1: Enchant elven short sword to +9.  Step 2: Take out your wand of
polymorph.  Step 3: Profit.)

That's not unbalanced, however, because you never get artifacts through
polymorph, two additional weapon pluses really aren't all THAT useful,
and you can't control what item you'll get out of it other than through
polymorphing until you get what you want.  There are no unlimited
sources of polymorph in the game, so is good.

> [5]: A greased ring should slide off your finger (unless the ring is
> cursed). --froggey

Why not even if the ring is cursed?  Extra uses for cans of grease are
a good thing, and they aren't exactly common.

> [6]: It should be possible to bribe some angry @ (eg. guards, priests)
> with money, with a luck penalty to lawfuls. --Pthag

Interesting idea!  Money needs more uses, and it would also help
lawfuls to do this since it would avoid the need to murder them after
angering them.  For priests the fee should be quite high, for guards
less so.  (Soldiers, too, perhaps should be bribable?  Croesus has to
be employing all those guys somehow, right?)

> [7]: NH balrogs explode cataclysmicly when they die, like D&D balors
> --GreyKnight

Not a good idea.  Balrogs come from Tolkien, where they certainly did
not explode (Gandalf would have told us about that).  I like exploding
monsters though, especially if they do enough damage to give even
high-level characters pause.  (Cocky bastards.)

> [8]: The Samurai player class should only be able to gain the title of
> "Ronin" when they have changed alignment (HoOA or altar conversion).
> --aristotle73

Interesting.  We already have the idea of rejected rank names (and
although I haven't checked to make sure, maybe even that very idea has
been implemented): http://bilious.homelinux.org/?13

> [9]: Frog, a jumping monster --lament

Excellent idea.  Are there any mythological or D&D frogs we could use
to make more difficult variants of base frogs?

> [10]: setrodox mentioned (and I agree) that it would be nice to see
> more information about magic missile deaths -- such as, killed by a
> magic missile cast by a <<insert monster type here>> --Lucca_ [how
> about: "killed by a Gnome with a wand of magic missile" -az]

Good idea.  Maybe "Killed by a gnome's wand of magic missile"?

> [11]: Quantum mechanics could carry a single random potion on them, or
> possibly a writing utensil (marker). --Ian-Keith

Why a random potion?  Is this a Brownian motion joke?  If they are
sometimes generated with a magic marker it should be very uncommon,
maybe around 5% of quantum mechanics.  That way, the player won't get
too magic markers if he reverse genocides quantum mechanics (I like the
idea, however, if giving players another option for reverse genociding
monsters).

> [12]: Force bolting a huge chunk of meat should result in a bunch of
> meatballs --PsyMar

Meat doesn't shatter like stone does though.  Hit it with concussive
force and you might bruise it, but not shatter it into pieces.  Ever
see Rocky?

